loper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-339131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8cff4ac340bd6e40ac5b1fa255e0ab63c82fcfbf829f19893dbe03e69080e7ab"} {"question" "q-339131" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-339131" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/2}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$   \n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}/2$ directly into the limit, we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}/2}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)) & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3\\cdot \\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+3\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8cff4ac340bd6e40ac5b1fa255e0ab63c82fcfbf829f19893dbe03e69080e7ab"} {"question" "q-152804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["text" "Undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3/2}\\frac{(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)-\\pi )^{2}}{2x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$ Since $\\frac{3}{2}\\notin [-1,1],$ this means that $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})$ is undefined.\n\nTherefore, our limit is undefined, too." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8cff4ac340bd6e40ac5b1fa255e0ab63c82fcfbf829f19893dbe03e69080e7ab"} {"question" "q-152761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-152761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "] ["text" "Undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844