egory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-339330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/e441953c2cefc6f817a64cb7ce0ebce53164ebb4d3974ae871b14d57450b5167.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }(\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x+1))=\\pi -(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-339330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8cff4ac340bd6e40ac5b1fa255e0ab63c82fcfbf829f19893dbe03e69080e7ab"} {"question" "q-339330" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca217960d2a9f3b1793de5172c49c6a4c8443844475fca7fa9cb61"} {"question" "q-339330" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9ff0f3558ca2